## reading notes
Iroh and WebTransport publishers were alive before the negatives and still alive after them (publishers-after-iroh-negatives and publishers-after-wt-negatives are alive/alive/alive). After-reads then received frames on each own path.
Iroh cross-root is subscribe-timeout exit 124, beside those living controls. WebTransport cross-root is unauthorized.
Iroh listen on the open alice token announced exactly two prefixes, alice/marker and bob/marker, both under the open root. The protected path was absent.
Alice's subscribe ** read bob/marker and bob's subscribe ** read alice/marker while both publishers were alive. That is same-root sibling read, which the grant allows.
Alice's WebTransport publish of bob/marker returned exit 0 and local bytes. It is not a relay refusal. Bob's own read still succeeded afterward.
Browser literal pathname kept ~open, connected, and received 21 frames / 399 bytes of mjolnir-relay-frame while the WebTransport publisher was alive. Encoded and double pathnames kept %7Eopen and %257Eopen and did not log moq-connected inside the wait.
The first frame on the shared bytes track was mjolnir-relay-frame from the WebTransport publisher, which writes that payload onto the same path the Iroh publisher announces.

## suite failures and toolchain
Default TMPDIR is /var/folders/2n/bmf28cr51l7456rv53ckjv7m0000gn/T (48 bytes). macOS sun_path is 104 bytes.
Reconcile thaw socket is btrfs_root plus a 22-character id and `_virtiofs.sock`. Under that TMPDIR the path is about 115 bytes, so :gen_tcp.listen fails. With TMPDIR=/tmp the same test path is about 71 bytes.
AIE guest_contract live_retry binds std::env::temp_dir()/aie-guest-<uuid>/admit.sock. Under the default TMPDIR that path is 106 bytes and UnixListener returns "path must be shorter than SUN_LEN". With TMPDIR=/tmp it is about 62 bytes.
TMPDIR=/tmp mix test test/reconcile_test.exs:266 test/mjolnir/aie/execute_test.exs:276 result: 2 passed, 36 excluded. No product source was changed.
Shell elixir is Homebrew 1.20.4 on OTP 29. mise lists 1.20.5-otp-27 but that binary is not what `elixir` runs. MIX_ENV=test compiles the router. MIX_ENV=dev mix compile --no-deps-check in the repo still fails on stale _build/dev beams with authorize_app/4. An isolated tree at /tmp/mj-dev-iso, with dependency beams symlinked and a fresh mjolnir build directory, ran MIX_ENV=dev mix compile --no-deps-check and produced Elixir.Mjolnir.API.Router.beam. That directory was removed afterward. The repo _build/dev cache was left as it was.
